am.android" /><meta property="al:android:url" content="https://www.instagram.com/p/DXXLOdkjJez/" /><meta property="fb:app_id" content="124024574287414" /><meta property="instapp:owner_user_id" content="4417812568" /><meta name="description" content="89 likes, 16 comments - mashrabiagallery le&#xa0; April 20, 2026: &quot;Miray Michel&#x2019;s &#x201c;Before the Colors Faded&#x201d; series emerged from an exploration of nostalgia and
the different layers of emotional landscapes connected to memory. The works reflect on moments and experiences as they move between presence, memory, and interpretation.

Miray Michel (b. 2000) is a self-taught artist born in Cairo and raised in Hurghada, where she currently resides. She holds a Bachelor&#x2019;s degree in Mass
Communication, majoring in Public Relations and Advertising, with a minor in Graphic Design.
She began expanding her practice in 2024, developing a body of work centering on collage, mixed media, and installation art, drawn to their limitless possibilities for
deconstruction and reconstruction, narratives and interpretations through visual materials. Her work functions as an ongoing dialogue and a form of resistance. Through layered compositions of found imagery and diverse materials, she investigates memory, vulnerability, and emotional perception, shaped by personal questions, reflections, and challenges that consume her, as well as her relationship with her surroundings and lived experiences.

Miray&#x2019;s work is on display until 30 Aprila within the tenth edition of &#x201c;My Favorite Things&#x201d;.

Miray Michel
Before the Colors Faded I, II, III
Digital Collage
80 x 58.36 cm
2025

